    "chunk_text": "The poems published in a 65 page soft cover book celebrate nature in vivid imagery. \u2018From an island in the lake, you rise all at once, to form aerial patterns.\u2019 Local words bring authenticity to the setting; \u2018by a waterhole under shady kumbuk trees I quietly watch \u2014 kingfishers cloaked in skill and turquoise.\u2019 John Gimlette, the author of \u2018Elephant Complex\u2019 is another international author who comments on the collection saying \u2018Exquisite poems from the heart and the forest. Nirma de Silva Wijeyeratne delicately evokes both the beauty and the sadness of life in these precious lines. I have so enjoyed reading these poems.\u2019\n\nThere are journeys where loss and grief are encountered. In a world of turmoil, moments of stillness show a longing for peace and quietness. The book offers hope as seen in landscape transformations, the poet\u2019s adjustment to life after the loss of her father and the sun setting aglow a goldfinch. Magical moments of simple things remain in the poet\u2019s mind. Ramya Chamalie Jirasinghe, poet and author, says \u2018This is a collection that I would carry with me as I go about my day, dipping into it at difficult times, after a harsh commute, when words of others jar, when the world feels desolate. By an evocative and sensitive poetic rendering of nature, place and life, these poems reaffirm the power of life to heal and regenerate.\u2019"
