    "chunk_size_bytes": 808,
    "chunk_text": "May Day does not belong to political parties. It belongs to the workers. It is a day earned through sacrifice, built on solidarity, and sustained by the collective will of the labour force. Its meaning cannot be allowed to erode into mere pageantry or political competition.\n\nThe call today is not for division, but for unity\u2014unity grounded not in political allegiance, but in shared interests as workers. The lessons of the past must guide the future. Only through such unity can the true spirit of May Day be restored.\n\nLet May Day once again become a day where the worker stands at the centre\u2014not as a prop in political display, but as the rightful bearer of its legacy and future.\n\n*The writer was\u00a0Former president CBEU, Then member of the convening committee to set up a national trade union center"
