    "md5": "d83cbf5df5c211705b304e4ca64b3856",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1224,
    "chunk_text": "Verit\u00e9 Research appoints Yanitra Kumaraguru as Head of Legal Research\n\nVerit\u00e9 Research has appointed Attorney-at-Law Yanitra Kumaraguru as the Team Lead of its Legal Research Division, which is dedicated to examining, analysing, and strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s legal frameworks and their enforcement.\n\nLast month, Kumaraguru led a public seminar at Verit\u00e9 Research\u2019s VThink! on the ethics of autonomous weapons in warfare.\n\nKumaraguru is an Attorney-at-Law of the Supreme Court of Sri Lanka and holds an LL.M. from Harvard University. She has previously served seven years as a Lecturer at the Faculty of Law, University of Colombo, and has consulted and published widely on topics including gender, technology and the law, human rights and humanitarian law.\n\nHer appointment comes at a time when Verit\u00e9 Research is expanding its legal research portfolio amid renewed opportunity for constitutional and institutional reform in Sri Lanka.\n\nUnder her leadership, the Legal Research Division will focus on areas such as technology and the law, access to justice, climate and the law, business and human rights, and civil, political, economic, social, and cultural rights\u2014approached through a robust intersectional lens."
  },
