    "chunk_size_bytes": 1762,
    "chunk_text": "Leadership Under Fire \u2013 Lessons from Dankotuwa \u2013 Episode 4\n\nLESSONS FROM MY CAREER: SYNTHESISING MANAGEMENT THEORY WITH PRACTICE \u2013 PART 36\n\nMy earlier episodes described my encounters with interfering politicians and labour challenges at Dankotuwa Porcelain. This chapter, however, deals with something more subtle\u2014but equally demanding: the complexity of managing a large, sophisticated organisation under constant pressure and uncertainty.\n\nWhen I re-joined Dankotuwa Porcelain PLC as a Director, both the Chairman and CEO were on the verge of leaving. I felt the board was not being properly informed. At board meetings, I began questioning even the data that was presented. That did not make me popular. In fact, I became something of a nuisance. The CEO left soon after.\n\nDuring this period, I was attending a programme in Japan when the company was selecting a new CEO. The Japanese director insisted on meeting me over lunch, even though I had reserved that day for my last-minute shopping. He wanted my opinion on the shortlisted candidate.\n\nAfter reviewing the profile, I felt strongly that the individual would be a misfit. Dankotuwa was not a simple operation. It was far more complex than a tile factory or a garment plant. With over 1,000 experienced workers, strong unions, and a demanding export market, the environment required not just competence, but resilience and maturity.\n\nThe board, however, took a different view and appointed him.\n\nThree days later, the Chairman called me. The new CEO had walked into his house with his resignation letter. The job had overwhelmed him. I said nothing. There was no need to say, \u201cI told you so.\u201d\n\nBy now, with the resignation of the Chairman, I was once again made the non-executive Chairman."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-05-10-islandlk-02433925",
    "num": "islandlk-02433925",
    "date_str": "2026-05-10",
    "description": "Leadership Under Fire \u2013 Lessons from Dankotuwa \u2013 Episode 4",
