    "md5": "6d362c860ac1c33ccd077e8fe6494e66",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1593,
    "chunk_text": "Public seminar on Annual Economic Review 2025\n\nThe Centre for Banking Studies (CBS) of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka (CBSL) has organised a public seminar to present and discuss the\u00a0Annual Economic Review 2025, a flagship publication that offers a comprehensive account of the nation\u2019s economic performance over the past year.\n\nScheduled for the morning of\u00a013 May 2026, the seminar will be held at the\u00a0Atrium of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka\u00a0on Janathipathi Mawatha, Colombo 01, from\u00a010.00 a.m. to 12.00 p.m.\u00a0The event will be conducted in English, ensuring accessibility to a broad audience of professionals, academics, students, and members of the general public with an interest in the country\u2019s economic trajectory.\n\nDr. L. R. C. Pathberiya, the Director of the Economic Research Department at CBSL. Dr. Pathberiya, a seasoned economist with deep expertise in macroeconomic analysis and policy formulation, is expected to deliver a nuanced interpretation of the data and trends captured in the\u00a0Annual Economic Review 2025.\n\nHis presentation will likely cover key indicators such as GDP growth, inflation dynamics, fiscal performance, external sector stability, and monetary policy outcomes.\n\nThose wishing to attend are requested to confirm their participation by\u00a04.00 p.m. on Tuesday, 12 May 2026.\n\nSL becoming a useful market signal for investors watching ZKTOR\u2019s South Asian push\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
