    "chunk_text": "Ambition \u2026 to be a famous singer\n\nHis ambition is to be a famous singer, one day, and Kalum Tharanga has the potential, and the experience, to succeed.\n\nHe says from 1996 to 2001 he played the octapad and sang with a band, called Scorpions.\n\nHe then moved to Dubai and joined the Sahara Flash music band.\n\nFourteen years later he teamed up Rhythm of Clarence as their main vocalist.\n\nKalum\u2019s overseas experience also include performances in the Maldives and India, as a vocalist, mainly doing the English hits.\n\nHe continues to play the drums and sings, as well, and, what\u2019s more, he has five original songs to his credit.\n\nHis one ambition, he says, is to be a famous singer and to do something special for his country.\n\nAligning graduate output with labour market needs:Why national policy intervention essential\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
