    "chunk_size_bytes": 1256,
    "chunk_text": "Dewasiri, who also owns and operates Devasiri Seafood and two hotels with around 25 rooms in the area said that most hotel and restaurant owners are in dire straits as many property owners have obtained bank loans.\n\nHe further noted that government support has not been sufficient to alleviate the crisis. Apart from that, hotel and restaurant owners are facing growing difficulties in repaying their bank loans.\n\n\u2018Regarding bank loans, we are not asking for a debt moratorium, but we need some relief to repay or restructure our loans, Dewasiri said.\n\nHe added that the government\u2019s main priority at this moment should be to promote tourism in regions unaffected by war-related tensions.\n\nDewasiri is a leading hotel and restaurant operator not only in Hikkaduwa but also in other popular tourist destinations, such as, Nuwara Eliya and Pasikudah, and is planning to expand operations to more areas across Sri Lanka.\n\nMIFL records Profit Before Tax of LKR 818 million in FY 2025-26\n\nHow could a modest sea passage like Hormuz hold the global economy hostage?\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
