    "md5": "ca2478629a552209fd8547ccf0b54309",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1428,
    "chunk_text": "Cabinet clears  $ 908,250 emergency antibiotic order amid rising hospital demand\n\nThe Cabinet of Ministers on Monday approved the procurement of an additional 865,000 vials of Meropenem, a critical antibiotic used in the treatment of severe bacterial infections, in response to rising demand across the country\u2019s public health system.\n\nThe fresh order, valued at $ 908,250 including freight charges, will be supplied by United Biotech Ltd., with the medicine manufactured by United Biotech (P) Ltd. in India.\n\nThe decision follows an earlier Cabinet approval granted on 21 October 2025 to procure 1.9 million vials of the same antibiotic for the country\u2019s healthcare network.\n\nAccording to the Government, the Medical Supplies Division subsequently requested an additional quantity equivalent to 45.53% of the original order due to a sharp increase in clinical demand.\n\nBased on the recommendation of the Standard High-Level Procurement Committee, Cabinet approved the proposal submitted by the Health Minister Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa to award the supplementary order to the same supplier at the original contracted unit price of $ 1.05 per vial.\n\nIt was noted that maintaining the original pricing helped avoid delays and additional procurement costs, while ensuring continuity in the supply of a life-saving antibiotic widely used in intensive care units (ICU) and emergency treatment of drug-resistant bacterial infections."
