    "md5": "2b7f1c5c1441eb68a0024588a100b800",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1086,
    "chunk_text": "National Police Commission term ends today amid pending new appointments\n\nThe term of office of the National Police Commission is scheduled to expire today, with the commission\u2019s final meeting taking place yesterday.\n\nDespite the expiry of its official term, the current members are expected to continue performing their duties until new appointments are made.\n\nThe present commission was appointed on 15 May 2023 and is chaired by retired Supreme Court Judge Lalith Ekanayake.\n\nUnder constitutional provisions, the President appoints the Chairperson and four members of the National Police Commission based on recommendations made by the Constitutional Council.\n\nThe National Police Commission is one of the nine independent commissions established under the 21st Amendment to the Constitution, which was passed by Parliament on 31 October 2022.\n\nThe commission functions as an independent oversight body with supervisory authority over the Sri Lanka Police and its officers.\n\nThe National Police Commission was first established in 2002 under the 17th Amendment to the Constitution."
